    "name": "TaskTracker API - Week 4",
    "description": "# TaskTracker API — Week 4: Authentication & Identity\n\n## Overview\n\nThis collection tests the authentication and identity layer added in  \nWeek 4, built on top of the Week 3 CRUD API.\n\n## Base URL\n\nAll requests use the `{{baseUrl}}` variable, set in the  \n`Local Development` environment to `http://localhost:5264`.\n\n## Authentication\n\n- Day 1: User registration (no auth required)\n    \n- Day 2+: Login issues a JWT; protected endpoints require this token  \n    as a Bearer token in the Authorization header\n    \n\n## Folder Structure\n\n- **Auth** — registration, login, and token-related endpoints\n    \n- **Tasks** — CRUD endpoints from Week 3, now behind authentication  \n    (added Day 2 onward)\n    \n\n## How to Run\n\n1. Start the API: `dotnet run` from `TaskTrackerApi/`\n    \n2. Select the `Local Development` environment (top-right dropdown)\n    \n3. Run requests in numerical order within each folder — later  \n    requests depend on data created by earlier ones",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "54406292",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/54406292-0b13c859-ba9f-4960-8fbd-917e5eee47d6?source=collection_link"
  },
